(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[15 1 "// Frame is a frame of a thread's stack (HES8 (a))."] [19 15 "// a case's slots; an apply frame's arguments"] [22 11 "// the thread's arena's top when the frame was pushed (arena.go)"] [30 8 "// restores the masking state n on return"] [35 8 "// keepAlive#'s value kept reachable while its action runs"] [38 1 "// Thread is a Haskell thread: its stack, its resumption, its masking state (0 unmasked, 1 masked"] [39 1 "// uninterruptibly, 2 masked interruptibly: getMaskingState#'s numbers)."] [50 23 "// what it waits on: *MVar, *Thunk, *sleep, stmWait, nil when runnable"] [51 23 "// the throwTo#s waiting for it to accept them (rts.go)"] [52 23 "// the TVars its transaction read (a retry's wake-up, the collector's reachability)"] [59 2 "// an interruptible block (MVar, delay, STM retry): an asynchronous exception may be delivered"] [63 1 "// Machine is hsi's machine: the loader, the address space, the threads."] [78 2 "// the weak pointers not yet dead, and the collector's memos of what code keeps alive (rts.go)"] [97 20 "// a pure primop's arguments"] [98 20 "// a thread's frames at most (SetStackLimit): StackOverflow past it"] [99 20 "// a tail call's arguments"] [110 1 "// hsFatal is an error of hsi itself (a class at the check: unimplemented, an impossible state)."] [113 1 "// exitNow ends the program (shutdownHaskellAndExit, an uncaught exception in the main thread)."] [120 1 "// NewMachine is a machine over the STG of the units in libs and the program in prog."] [159 1 "// blockedE is returned by a node whose thread blocked: its resumption is set already."] [162 1 "// enterValue evaluates a value: a thunk entered, anything else returned."] [171 1 "// enter evaluates a thunk: its value, or its code under an update frame, the thunk blackholed."] [189 3 "// another thread evaluates it: wait for its update; a transaction aborts first and reruns from its start"] [190 3 "// after the wake-up (review 189, F2, the user's decision: the other threads never see its writes)"] [208 4 "// two update frames in a row (the lower thunk's evaluation is entering this one): squeezed as GHC's"] [209 4 "// stack squeezing does, the lower thunk an indirection to this one, one frame for both (cgrun060 at"] [210 4 "// +RTS -K64k)"] [211 4 "// (the lower thunks kept blackholed in the frame's env, updated, raised or reverted with it)"] [219 4 "// evaluated in place (newThunkN)"] [228 1 "// update overwrites a thunk with its value."] [232 30 "// the fields and the frame may live in the thunk's own allocation"] [243 1 "// apply calls f with args (eval/apply: exact, partial, over-saturated)."] [283 1 "// ApplyV applies a value to values (a thread's start, a primop's callback)."] [293 1 "// ret handles the top frame on a return."] [311 4 "// a queued throwTo# delivered at the unmasking, its value lost as GHC's"] [324 1 "// raiseLam is the code of a thunk whose evaluation raised: entered, it raises again."] [327 1 "// RaiseFree raises its frame's first slot."] [334 1 "// raise raises a synchronous exception (raise#, raiseIO#): the stack unwound to the nearest catch"] [335 1 "// frame, the thunks under evaluation on the way updated to raise it again."] [340 1 "// raiseAsync raises an asynchronous exception in the current thread: the thunks under evaluation on"] [341 1 "// the way reverted to unevaluated (GHC freezes them; the same results)."] [368 5 "// an asynchronous exception is not catchSTM#'s: its nested writes undone, on (review 189, F9)"] [383 1 "// uncaught ends a thread whose exception reached the bottom of its stack (forkIO's and runMainIO's own"] [384 1 "// handlers catch everything, so only a thread started without them gets here: one killed before it ran,"] [385 1 "// which ends silently, as GHC's)."] [393 2 "// a thread killed before it started (forkIO's handler not yet on its stack) ends silently, as GHC's"] [396 1 "// ---- threads ----"] [406 1 "// wake makes a blocked thread runnable."] [416 1 "// block stops the current thread until it is woken; on waking it returns from the blocked call"] [417 1 "// (with the return registers its waker sets) or runs e."] [424 3 "// a queued throwTo# delivered as the thread blocks interruptibly (threadPaused's"] [425 3 "// maybePerformBlockedException; review 189, F5)"] [433 1 "// unblock takes a blocked thread out of what it waits on."] [466 3 "// its throwTo# revoked"] [471 2 "// an interrupted MVar operation leaves no state (review 189, F4)"] [477 1 "// Run runs the program's :Main.main and returns its exit status."] [515 1 "// where describes the current thread's stack for an error message."] [542 1 "// schedule runs threads until until is done (or every thread is)."] [593 1 "// deadlock is GHC's scheduleDetectDeadlock when no thread can run and none waits for time: a collection (rts.go's"] [594 1 "// gc) resurrects the blocked threads no root reaches; when it resurrects none, the main thread, blocked, gets"] [595 1 "// NonTermination (the non-threaded RTS's last resort). False: nothing to do (hsi stops)."] [607 1 "// runSlice runs t for a time slice, or until it blocks or ends."] [620 5 "// GHC's threadStackOverflow: StackOverflow raised in the thread, asynchronously"] [624 39 "// a transaction is not preempted (HES9 (a))"] [644 1 "// shutdown flushes the standard handles (hs_exit's flushStdHandles) and is the exit status."] [656 1 "// Exit is the program's end requested by shutdownHaskellAndExit: the handles flushed first."] [670 1 "// CFunctions are the C functions hsi's table has."] [679 1 "// PrimopNames are the primops hsi implements."] [688 1 "// Loaded is the number of modules loaded, LoadedBytes their forms' size, Steps the nodes run (by slices)."] [693 1 "// defaultStackFrames is a thread's frames at most without -K: 2 GiB of frames (GHC's default is 80 % of the host's"] [694 1 "// memory, which hsi's frames, larger than GHC's words, would reach later than GHC; a bound keeps an endless recursion"] [695 1 "// from taking the host: the review of HE4d's runs). Loop's 3,000,000-deep chain needs about 10 million."] [698 1 "// frameBytes is a frame's size, the unit -K's bytes are counted in (GHC counts its stack's words; a frame of hsi's"] [699 1 "// holds what a few of GHC's words do, so a -K limit is reached at a comparable depth, not the same one)."] [702 1 "// SetStackLimit sets a thread's stack limit to bytes (+RTS -K)."] [711 1 "// unwindThunk is a thunk under evaluation an exception unwinds: reverted to unevaluated (asynchronous), or made to raise"] [712 1 "// again (synchronous); its waiters woken."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[164 24] [176 27] [207 18] [235 23] [312 36] [372 37] [426 35] [484 20] [524 27] [524 44] [600 17] [722 24]]} (go/file "machine.go" :imports [


